{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "mos-farblit-byte-load-legalization",
  "title": "Combined native-width stack rejects a farblit absolute byte load",
  "status": "fixed",
  "summary": "Patch 0066 repairs the farblit byte-load legalization failure: 0061 eagerly selects an extending far byte load after queuing its generic G_LOAD, and the in-place absolute rewrite leaves that target pseudo on the generic worklist. Build-and-erase removes the queued instruction. The unchanged historical source fails on the preserved baseline and passes with the repair; eight farblit/pressure emulator runs pass.",
  "report": "docs/plans/2026-09-26-mos-carry-scheduling.md",
  "reproducer_origin": "original",
  "attribution": [
    "OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session 01a0dd01-d72e-76f2-bf27-a796e0f7d994: observation during carry-scheduling validation and baseline capture. Original fixture attribution remains in the increment-2 plan.",
    "OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session 01a0e126-2178-79f3-adba-51b951fb1f96. Cause isolation, 0066 repair, direct MIR regression, preserved-input comparison and runtime validation.",
    "OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra, high reasoning effort; session 01a0e529-62c6-7fc2-a0c6-357800272c63: instruction-shape reconciliation, reconstructed MIR control, and repeated runtime checks; no change to compiler or gate expectations."
  ],
  "unknowns": "The opcode-count deficit is reconciled in the September 28 investigation: native rdw replaces one/two indexed byte loads, while cp8 A16 remains outside the local range proof. The shell gate still exits 1 at unchanged minima 3/6 (observed 2/5); all eight runtime assertions pass on the preserved 0066 candidate. Replacing the aggregate gate and measuring indexed native-word/copy profitability remain separate work. No exact-upstream applicability or independent review is claimed.",
