    "reconciliation_2026_09_27": {
      "decision": "Continue the existing canonical record. The September 26 preserved compiler hash is unchanged and reproduces the same absolute-byte diagnostic. The pre-edit source is retained as MOSLegalizerInfo.original.cpp.gz. The 0061 eager extended-byte path publishes G_LOAD to the worklist, then the 0001 in-place absolute-address rewrite turns the queued instruction into a target pseudo without erasing it. Removing only that eager block makes the original and reduced inputs pass. 0066 instead builds the target pseudo and erases the generic instruction, retaining eager addressing and memory operands. 0062 and carry scheduling are not required to explain this failure. The post-edit live source matches the tested candidate. No upstream submission is prepared.",
      "evidence": {
        "path": "docs/defects/evidence/2026-09-27-farblit-byte-load/prior-work.json",
        "sha256": "231e6cee19740088dcdea90dd169af3f79b1ca4179a0b5f84f5c704a69029c33"
      }
    },
    "reconciliation_2026_09_28": {
      "decision": "Append to the existing legalization record as instruction-shape reconciliation; no new compiler defect or status change. 0002 contains runtime byte index folding, 0061 adds global long,X, 0062 native words, and 0066 repairs legalizer worklist handling. The tested binary is the preserved September 27 candidate, not the current installed toolchain. Fresh disassemblies and ROMs match the retained evidence. Reconstructed MIR control isolates rdw byte splitting; it is not a historical build.",
      "evidence": {
