  "resolution": {
    "change": "patches/llvm-mos/0066-mos-far-extload-worklist.patch",
    "causal_explanation": "MOSLegalizerInfo::legalizeLoad rewrites G_ZEXTLOAD/G_SEXTLOAD to G_LOAD and calls changedInstr, queuing it for legalization. Patch 0061 then selects the far address immediately. tryFarAbsoluteAddressing mutated that same queued instruction to G_LOAD_FAR_ABS; LegalizerWorkListManager::changingInstr does not remove it and changedInstr only inserts generic opcodes. A target pseudo was therefore processed as generic. Replacing it with a new target instruction and erasing the generic one clears the pending worklist entry and preserves all memory references.",
    "trigger_check": "The unchanged September 26 source.i and reduced direct G_ZEXTLOAD/G_SEXTLOAD MIR fail with the preserved baseline. Plain byte-return C passes as a control. Disabling only the 0061 eager-selection block passes the original input. With eager selection retained and 0066 applied, the original source passes at Os/O2 in a16/xy16, and direct MIR passes in byte/a16/xy16 modes. Farblit and farblit_press return host oracles on MAME and bsnes-jg in both native modes.",
    "regression": {
      "path": "docs/defects/evidence/2026-09-26-farblit-byte-load/source.i",
